% =====================================================================
% refs.bib — master bibliography for the CAPR project
%
% This file is the single source of truth for citations across all
% project markdown (DEV_NOTES.md, dossiers, README sections) and the
% forthcoming LaTeX write-up. Cite from Markdown using pandoc-style
% keys: [@HoggPhonology1992], [@HoggGrammar1992, §4.11], [-@Ringe2006] (suppress author).
% Pandoc converts these directly to biblatex \autocite{} commands.
%
% Conventions
% -----------
% * Citekey format: <FirstAuthorSurname><Year>[<disambig>]
%   - Single author:        Campbell1959
%   - Joint authorship:     RingeTaylor2014, KlugeSeebold2011
%   - Multiple a year:      Stiles1986a, Stiles1986b
%   - Posthumous editions:  use the year of the cited edition
%     (e.g. SieversBrunner1965 for Sievers/Brunner 3rd ed.).
% * Prefer @book / @article / @incollection / @phdthesis etc. as
%   appropriate. Use @misc only when nothing else fits.
% * Fields marked "% TODO:" need verification before final
%   publication; the entry is usable in draft prose meanwhile.
% * Local file pointer: include  file = {docs/references/<stem>.pdf}
%   so editors / readers can resolve the PDF.
% =====================================================================

% =====================================================================
% Primary handbooks (PGmc → OE phonology and morphology)
% =====================================================================

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------
% The two distinct works published by Richard M. Hogg in 1992
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------
% CAPR formerly cited both under a single key `Hogg1992`, which conflated
% them. That key has been retired; cite one of the explicit keys below.
%
%   HoggGrammar1992    = A Grammar of Old English, vol. 1: Phonology
%                        (Blackwell). Sole-authored. Cited by section
%                        (§4.11, §5.10, §7.18 ...). The local witness is
%                        the 2011 Wiley-Blackwell paperback, which is the
%                        same text but REPAGINATED: 1992 page ~= 2011
%                        page + 2 (identical up to about p. 24).
%
%   HoggCHEL1992       = The Cambridge History of the English Language,
%                        vol. I, which Hogg EDITED. Multi-author; cite the
%                        individual chapter authors below, not the volume,
%                        whenever a page locator is given.
%
% Chapter authorship of HoggCHEL1992 (page ranges):
%   ch. 1 Introduction .................. Hogg ............ pp.   1-- 25
%   ch. 2 The Place of English .......... Bammesberger .... pp.  26-- 66
%   ch. 3 Phonology and Morphology ...... Hogg ............ pp.  67--167
%   ch. 4 Syntax ........................ Traugott ........ pp. 168--289
%   ch. 5 Semantics and Vocabulary ...... Kastovsky ....... pp. 290--407
%   ch. 6 Old English Dialects .......... Toon ............ pp. 409--451
%   ch. 7 Onomastics .................... Clark ........... pp. 452--487
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------

